Answers of the JSON API of the original CMS (Contest Management System,
https://github.com/cms-dev/cms, AGPL-3.0-or-later; copyright © the CMS
contributors), version 1.6.dev0 (commit 1914a5a), for the demo contest of
testdata/dumps/demo (exported from that same installation), recorded on
2026-10-15. TestCMSAPI (api_test.go) replays every step against this site and
compares the status codes and the JSON values.

  cms.json            the steps (tools/steps.py: SQL to run first, request,
                      login_data to send) and CMS's answer to each: status,
                      Content-Type, JSON body (or the start of an HTML body)
                      and, for submissions, the official flag, language and
                      comment stored. login_data values are replaced by
                      "<login_data>" ("<sent login_data>" when CMS returned
                      the header it received), and the ids of new
                      submissions by "<id:N>" (also in later lists).
  details.sql         the score details the steps use, computed with CMS's
                      own GroupMin and Sum (tools/gen_details.py): alice's
                      submission on sum (testcase 000 public, the rest
                      private) and a new submission of alice on half; run
                      on both databases before the steps.
  tools/              the scripts: gen_details.py (run with CMS's Python,
                      CMS_CONFIG set), steps.py and record_api.py
                      (record_api.py OUT.json [BASE] [DBURL], against a
                      CMS with contest_admin_token = "test-admin-token"
                      whose database has details.sql applied).

Documented differences (TestCMSAPI expects ours instead):
  - the public details of a subtask with private testcases have no score
    keys; CMS's get_json_details fails on them (500), ours returns the
    subtask without them (internal/grading/scoretype);
  - JSON is compact and numbers keep their value, not their spelling (40.0
    may be written 40).
